@* CultureReactiveBody — BETA-8-I18N-#4 (see test-results/r8/A8-settings.md).

   A thin wrapper that hosts a single RenderFragment and re-renders
   whenever the @key (typically the current culture) changes.
   Used by the layouts' @Body slot so the child page is force-remounted
   on every culture change — without this, the page text stays in
   the language it was first rendered in, even after the user picks
   a new language in the topbar.

   Blazor's layout → @Body cascade only re-invokes the @Body
   RenderFragment when the route changes. A culture change re-renders
   the layout (so the topbar, sidebar, and profile menu re-localise)
   but the @Body is not re-invoked. The @key attribute is the only
   way to force a remount from outside the child component. *@

@implements IDisposable
@using Cardscape.Web.Services
@inject CultureSwitcher Culture

@ChildContent

@code {
    /// <summary>The child fragment to render. The layout passes its
    /// own @Body here.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Subscribes to culture changes so the wrapping
    /// fragment re-renders (and any keyed children are diffed
    /// against the new key).</summary>
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        Culture.Changed += OnCultureChanged;
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        Culture.Changed -= OnCultureChanged;
        GC.SuppressFinalize(this);
    }

    private void OnCultureChanged() => InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
}
